<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n45040" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">spīrābĭlis</span></b> ,
		e, adj.
		spiro, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>that may be breathed</i>, <i>good to
			breathe</i>, <i>breathable</i>, <i>respirable.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">terra circumfusa undique est hac animali
					spirabilique naturā, cui nomen est aër,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					N. D. 2, 36, 91</span></i>
			; cf. <i><span class="en">id. ib. 2, 6, 18</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Tusc.
				1, 17, 40</span></i>; <i><span class="en">1, 29,
			70</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b> * </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<i>Pass.</i>, <i>that serves to sustain
				life</i>, <i>vital</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">per sidera testor, caeli spirabile lumen,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 3, 600</span></i>
			.—* </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<i>Act.</i>, <i>that can breathe</i>,
				<i>fitted for breathing</i>, <i>respiratory</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">viscera,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					9, 7, 6, § 17</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
</div>